cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Lean-Verified Session Protocols as the Security Boundary of LLM Agent Swarms"
message: "If you use this software or its ideas, please cite the paper."
authors:
  - given-names: Mauricio
    family-names: Neubecker
    affiliation: "Technical University of Munich; Safe AI Germany"
  - given-names: Tim
    family-names: Würfl
    affiliation: "Technical University of Munich; Safe AI Germany"
  - given-names: Maximilian
    family-names: Eder
    affiliation: "Technical University of Munich; Safe AI Germany"
abstract: >-
  A swarm runtime in which inter-agent messages are typed by a Lean-4-checked multiparty session protocol
  and enforced at runtime by a verified reference monitor, so untrusted LLM agents can only communicate in
  ways the declared protocol allows.
keywords: [multi-agent systems, LLM agents, session types, Lean 4, reference monitor, prompt injection, AI safety]
license: Apache-2.0
